<h1>Editor Features</h1>

<h2>Keyboard shortcuts</h2>

<p>All shortcuts use <strong>Ctrl</strong> on Windows/Linux and <strong>Cmd</strong> on macOS. They work whenever the editor has focus.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Shortcut</th><th>Action</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+K</strong></td><td>Insert or edit link. If the cursor is inside an existing link, the dialog pre-fills with the current URL and the whole link is replaced on OK. If text is selected, that selection becomes the link text. The dialog supports full URLs, hand-typed relative paths, and a picker of other HD documents in the same publish group.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+B</strong></td><td>Bold (toggle).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+I</strong></td><td>Italic (toggle).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+U</strong></td><td>Underline (toggle).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+E</strong></td><td>Inline code (toggle).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Shift+X</strong></td><td>Strikethrough (toggle).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Alt+1</strong> … <strong>Ctrl+Alt+6</strong></td><td>Set the current block to a heading of level 1–6.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Alt+0</strong></td><td>Set the current block back to a paragraph.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Shift+8</strong></td><td>Toggle bullet list.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Shift+7</strong></td><td>Toggle numbered list.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Shift+B</strong></td><td>Toggle blockquote.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Z</strong> / <strong>Ctrl+Shift+Z</strong></td><td>Undo / Redo.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> → "HD: Copy as Markdown"</td><td>Copy the current document's body as Markdown.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>The toolbar exposes the same actions as visible buttons — the shortcuts are an accelerator, not a replacement. The toolbar stays fixed at the top of the editor pane as you scroll, so it's always reachable.</p>

<h2>Toolbar</h2><p>Headings (H1–H3 buttons; H4–H6 via Markdown shortcuts), bold, italic, underline, inline code, code block, link, bullet list, ordered list, blockquote, horizontal rule, insert table.</p><h2>Tables</h2><p>HD tables support the full HTML capability set — <code>colspan</code>, <code>rowspan</code>, multi-paragraph cells, inline styles, header rows and columns. The editor provides three ways to manipulate them.</p><h3>Hover insert</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Columns</strong>: hover near the top of a table — within ~28 px above the top edge or anywhere in the header row — to see <strong>+</strong> buttons at every column boundary, including far left and far right. Click any one to insert a column at that boundary.</p></li><li><p><strong>Rows</strong>: hover near the left of a table to see <strong>+</strong> buttons at every row boundary, including above the first row and below the last. Click to insert a row.</p></li></ul><h3>Right-click menu</h3><p>Right-click any table cell for the full menu:</p><ul><li><p>Insert column before / after / delete column</p></li><li><p>Insert row above / below / delete row</p></li><li><p>Toggle header row / header column</p></li><li><p>Delete table</p></li></ul><h3>Resize columns</h3><p>Hover within a couple of pixels of a vertical column boundary — the cursor changes to a horizontal resize indicator. Drag to resize. The chosen widths are stored as inline <code>style</code>/<code>colwidth</code> attributes and round-trip with the document.</p><h2>Paste behavior</h2><p>The paste handler dispatches based on clipboard content type, in this order:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Image file</strong> — saved to the document's asset folder as <code>image-N.&lt;ext&gt;</code>; an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> reference with the bare filename is inserted at the cursor.</p></li><li><p><strong>HTML</strong> — sanitized against the HD allow-list (disallowed elements are unwrapped, disallowed attributes stripped) and inserted. Office-style <code>StartFragment</code> / <code>EndFragment</code> wrappers are stripped first.</p></li><li><p><strong>Markdown-flavored plain text</strong> — detected by a conservative heuristic (needs at least two distinct Markdown markers across headings, lists, code fences, links, bold, tables); converted via <code>marked</code>, sanitized, inserted.</p></li><li><p><strong>Plain text</strong> — falls through to the editor's default plain-text handling. No code-block wrapping.</p></li></ol><h2>Clipboard out</h2><p><strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> → "<strong>HD: Copy as Markdown</strong>" copies the document's body as Markdown. Elements that round-trip cleanly are emitted as Markdown; everything else is emitted as raw HTML inside the Markdown so no content is lost. The per-element round-trip status is documented in <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="./format-spec.hd">format-spec.hd</a>.</p><h2>Document identity</h2><p>Every <code>.hd</code> file gets a 22-character base62 <code>id</code> in its frontmatter on first open. The id is stable across renames and moves and is what asset folders are keyed by.</p><ul><li><p>To force regeneration (e.g., when using a template), clear the <code>id:</code> value and reopen the file.</p></li><li><p>If you duplicate an <code>.hd</code> file in the explorer, the editor detects the duplicate id on next open and regenerates the new file's id automatically.</p></li></ul><h2>Format version</h2><p>Documents carry a <code>version</code> field in their frontmatter. The current version is <code>1</code>. The editor injects <code>version: 1</code> on first open if the field is missing. A missing or absent version is interpreted as the latest version.</p>